<item>
            <title>[KYLIN-6055] Empty `dimension_range_info_map` After Building Model with Secondary Partition Causes Query to Fail Filtering by Dimension</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KYLIN-6055</link>
                <project id="12316121" key="KYLIN">Kylin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;For the same model without secondary partitioning, the dimension min/max in `dimension_range_info_map` is generated correctly after building.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/13074987/13074987_image-2025-02-25-16-56-39-917.png&quot; height=&quot;263&quot; width=&quot;427&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For the same model with secondary partitioning, the dimension min/max in `dimension_range_info_map` is not generated correctly after building.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/13074986/13074986_image-2025-02-25-16-57-04-319.png&quot; height=&quot;190&quot; width=&quot;446&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Impact: For query scenarios with only regular dimension filters and no partition column filters, the query will scan the entire data after model building, and query performance cannot be guaranteed.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="13609664">KYLIN-6055</key>
            <summary>Empty `dimension_range_info_map` After Building Model with Secondary Partition Causes Query to Fail Filtering by Dimension</summary>
